WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.502
A normalized operational database and an analytical model solve different problems.

00:00:05.502 --> 00:00:10.307
OLTP systems focus on safe day-to-day transactions.

00:00:10.307 --> 00:00:17.342
They reduce duplicated facts, protect updates, and use keys and constraints to preserve integrity.

00:00:17.342 --> 00:00:21.922
Analytical models focus on understandable, efficient reporting.

00:00:21.922 --> 00:00:27.622
Fact tables store measurable events, while dimensions provide descriptive context.

00:00:27.622 --> 00:00:35.277
That means a star schema may intentionally repeat some descriptive values in ways an operational schema would

00:00:35.277 --> 00:00:40.357
avoid. The important point is that dimensional modeling complements the normalized source.

00:00:40.357 --> 00:00:43.647
It does not excuse poor operational design.

00:00:43.647 --> 00:00:49.437
A trustworthy analytical model is easier to build when the source system has clear grain,

00:00:49.437 --> 00:00:55.497
reliable identifiers, controlled relationships, and well-enforced business rules.

00:00:55.497 --> 00:00:59.912
Operational and analytical models optimize for different work.

00:00:59.912 --> 00:01:07.832
An OLTP schema protects transactional consistency, while a star schema often makes reporting simpler and

00:01:07.832 --> 00:01:11.107
faster. A mature data platform may intentionally use both:

00:01:11.107 --> 00:01:15.559
normalized operational sources feeding dimensional analytical models.
